{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 branch 2 IMPLEMENTED and pushed for review as Gerrit change **2674** — \"Say what keeps\ngate_scratch_mount in step\" (`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2674`), commit\n`f442bffa3178`, trailer `rebar-ticket: ad8d-4274-ef43-4f44` (`rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev\nHEAD` resolves it). NOT submitted and this ticket is NOT closed: policy is `Verified +1` before a\nclose, and the operator is spacing submits deliberately.\n\n**What the audit found while writing it, which is finer-grained than F6 states.** F6 says the\nvalue \"is not actually single-sourced\". That is right, but the split is 2/2, not 4/0 — worth\nrecording because the corrected prose had to be accurate rather than merely less wrong:\n\n- DERIVED from `var.gate_scratch_mount` (changing the default DOES move these):\n  - `infra/terraform/user_data.sh:214`'s `GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT=\"${gate_scratch_mount}\"`, fed by\n    `infra/terraform/main.tf:91`'s `gate_scratch_mount = var.gate_scratch_mount` into\n    `templatefile`.\n  - `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:298`'s `mount = var.gate_scratch_mount` — the\n    CloudWatch alarm dimension.\n- HARDCODED literals (changing the default does NOT move these):\n  - `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:268-269` — `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` and `TMPDIR`.\n  - `infra/scripts/observability.sh:72` —\n    `GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT=\"${GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT:-/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch}\"`, which the df probe\n    at `:233` and the metric dimension at `:238` read.\n\nSo the old sentence was not simply imprecise; it was actively misleading for exactly the two\nconsumers a `terraform apply` cannot reach. The replacement names which two derive, which two must\nbe updated alongside, and — because \"what stops these drifting?\" is the reader's real next question\n— that the answer is `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`, which pins all four against one\n`SCRATCH_MOUNT` constant so an isolated edit fails offline rather than on a host. Written to\ndescribe today's tree, not an aspiration: it does not claim the value will become single-sourced.\n\nBranch 1 (deriving the compose value) was deliberately NOT taken — it is a design change to how\n`docker-compose.yml` is templated, it is not what AC5 asks for, and it does not belong inside a bug\nfix. The commit message says so, so the next reader does not mistake the prose fix for the whole\nanswer.\n\nChecks run in a clean worktree at `origin/main` (`0033662b5534`): `terraform fmt -check -diff`\nclean; `terraform validate` \"Success! The configuration is valid.\" after `terraform init\n-backend=false -input=false` (no backend, no state access, **no apply**);\n`pytest tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py\ntests/unit/test_user_data_device_resolution_d614.py\ntests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py` → 56 passed, 7 skipped. The commit gate\n(pre-commit: 50/72 wrap, ruff, mypy) passed; DCO sign-off present.\n\n**AC5 remains unticked on purpose.** It becomes tickable when 2674 is `Verified +1` and merged —\nnot before — and the close is blocked until then by the same precheck that refused earlier. Nothing\nwas forced or bypassed at any point."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788605619335714260,"uuid":"71b562ec-e074-4974-9852-029488480307"}